<title>JAPAN: Dlr falls to 111.80 yen in Tokyo, lowest since Nov.</title>
<headline>Dlr falls to 111.80 yen in Tokyo, lowest since Nov.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The dollar fell to 111.80 yen around midday in Tokyo on Monday, the lowest level since November 25, 1996, currency traders said.</p>
<p>The dollar recovered slightly to be quoted at 112.10/20 yen as of 0313 GMT.</p>
<p>The dollar fell amid sentiment that Japan's April current account surplus data due on Wednesday will show a substantial rise, dealers said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-9780</p>
</text>
